Subject: [PATCH] 10048: Pass Go complex numbers in two float registers

Pass Go complex numbers in two float registers

Map Go complex64/complex128 (RTTI kinds and DWARF base types tagged with
a Go kind) to complex data types, and allocate them like Go's ABI does:
real and imaginary parts in two float registers, or both on the stack.

Pass the encoding to the Go base type test helper
